Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
From the master equations to the zero-frequency QNM coefficients\
\>", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002546051334445*^9, 
  4.002546056340289*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8ad03f6f-4a55-481b-8e9a-\
3d561835400e"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook uses the results of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Derive_the_equations.nb\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
section \"Mikel solutions\", as its starting point. It specializes the \
coupled master equations to zero frequency, rewrites them in the variables of \
the zero-frequency QNM solver \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]QNMsZeroFrequency.nb\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], and extracts the coefficients of the quadratic \
momentum eigenvalue problem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002546074110523*^9, 4.002546077275914*^9}, {
  4.0025465126170683`*^9, 
  4.002546518368874*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b046a716-5130-4e5c-99ed-\
a939f876af03"],

Cell["\<\
The starting equations already correspond to \[Chi] = 1 and use the full \
scalar potential V. The general-\[Chi] system in \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Derive_the_equations.nb\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] uses a \
shifted potential; its comparison section applies V -> V + 3/\[Chi].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0025460270517673`*^9, 4.002546039244619*^9}, {
  4.002546524751783*^9, 
  4.002546532894506*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50b728f9-c610-4539-83b7-\
64b4843907b7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Starting equations from Derive_the_equations.nb", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b9a0d39f-8401-4357-8744-cc820d67f7f7"],

Cell["\<\
The following input cell is copied from the \"Mikel solutions\" section. \
ZPhiMikel and Z2Mikel are left-hand sides of equations set equal to zero; \
they retain finite frequency and momentum.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8666f288-b05e-4bda-b590-ec4bcdc58e43"],

